| Provider | https://rail-pay.vercel.app/provider |
| Code | https://github.com/lozentrad3s/rail |

Monad testnet, chain 10143. Addresses in `docs/DEPLOYMENTS.md`, which records why each redeployment
happened and what was measured to justify it.

### Trying it

**As a sender:** open the chat, `add mum`, choose **Test Bank (test mode only)** and any account
number, then `send 50k to mum` and approve on your phone.

**As a provider:** `/provider`, connect a wallet, stake at least $100, and bid inside the 45-second
commit window.

---

## 8. What is not finished

Stated plainly, because a judge will find these anyway.

- **CRE simulation is unrun.** The workflow is written and its rules are tested, but
  `cre workflow simulate` requires authentication and Chainlink's auth service returns a 500 on token
  refresh. Not our bug, and not worked around.
- **WhatsApp is pending Meta's business verification.** The transport is built and tested.
- **History is per-device.** The 100-block log cap means a sender's dashboard reads orders this
  device recorded. The honest fix is the indexer or a relayer endpoint keyed by sender.
- **Paystack is in test mode**, which permits three live bank resolves per day. Hence the test bank.
- **No audit.** Testnet, play money, and nobody should put real savings behind it yet.

---

*Rail is not another fintech promising a better rate. It is the mechanism that makes three hundred
of them compete for one transfer, in the open, and hands the difference back to the person who sent
it.*
